  "executive_briefing": "The digital asset landscape has entered a critical consolidation phase as of June 2026, centered on the legislative endgame of the CLARITY Act. With the Senate Banking Committee's 15-9 approval and a reported move toward a full floor vote, the U.S. is nearing a definitive regulatory framework that formally distinguishes Bitcoin and Ethereum from securities. This legislative milestone is a primary driver behind a structural supply squeeze; institutional entities now control over 9% of the total Bitcoin supply, with IBIT options alone catalyzing $32.8 billion in recent inflows. Simultaneously, the industry is aggressively pivoting away from 'wrapped' assets toward trustless, native-to-native cross-chain protocols like THORChain and deBridge, effectively integrating Bitcoin\u2019s liquidity into the broader DeFi ecosystem without the systemic risk of centralized bridges.",
